# **`psn_t3_expired`** — the fourth of `player_state_normal`'s countdowns
# reaching zero, and the only one of the four that clears something on its way
# out (`$80:D2DF  DEC $56 : BNE : STZ $54`).
#
# **The mechanism had to be understood before the input, because the obvious
# ones cannot do it.** `$56` is a per-state timer: states 2, 4 and 6 each arm
# their own copy and each end exactly when it runs out, inside that state. So
# `$80:D2DF` had executed **zero times in 27,698 calls** — by the time state 0
# runs, `$56` is always already zero. The one site that hands a live countdown
# to state 0 is `$80:EB23`, item slot 1's entry in the `JMP ($EB07,X)` table:
#
#     $80:EB23  LDA #$8000 : STA $54
#     $80:EB28  LDA #$0352 : STA $56
#
# `$80:EAEC  LDA $4E : ORA $70 : BNE` refuses the item unless `$70` is zero, so
# it is used from state 0 and stays there, and its 850 frames count down in
# `player_state_normal` until the fourth countdown clears the `$8000` this set.
# That pairing — `$54` armed there, cleared here — is what the branch is *for*,
# and neither routine says so alone.
#
# Item slot 1 is collision id `$22`, object type `$0A`, and nine are placed in
# the cartridge: levels 3, 12 (two), 19 (two), 25, 29, 41 and 47. Only three of
# those have a password, and only one of the three has a route — `zamn_assets
# route` still refuses level 25's (128,694) and level 41's (1590,123) from their
# own movies' starts. So the branch hangs on one object in level 29.
#
# **GLZJ is level 29**, and this is 47 legs of `tools/fit_route.py` from the
# spawn at (277,1435) to the object at (553,212).
#
# It is also the first movie cut after the search's box was corrected, and the
# reason the correction happened. `$80:AE14` biases **both** axes before
# dividing — `SBC #$0009` on the column, `SBC #$0008` on the row — and the
# search had modelled only the row's, which put its box a tile right of the
# game's. The old plan died on leg 5, holding `Up` at (973,1475): two pixels and
# a wall, where the search said 248 px were clear. `zamn_assets probe 30 973
# 1475 --to 973 1227` names the tile that stops him — col 120, row 182,
# attribute `$0003` — and the corrected plan goes eight pixels right first.
#
# The tail, from `--watch`:
#
#     4301  $1D0E 0 -> 1                 he walks onto the object
#     4362  $1CC0 7 -> 1                 A cycles off the first-aid kit onto it
#     4386  $54 = $8000, $56 = 849, and $1CC0 back to 7: X spends it, the slot
#           empties, and the selection moves to the only one left
#     5235  $56 -> 0 and $54 -> 0 in the same frame — the branch
#
# 849 frames of countdown and not one of them interrupted, which is the other
# half of the input: the item is spent standing where the route ended, and
# anything that took him out of state 0 would have taken the countdown with it.
#
# `zamn_cosim verify -f 5300` checks 300,136 calls with nothing diverged.

